    "checklist": {
      "reviewed": 4,
      "passRate": 94,
      "items": {
        "A breadcrumb leads back to the contracts list and ends with the contract number, and the header shows the contract number, vendor name, a status badge with text, and at most four key fields (such as value, start and end date)": 100,
        "The header has one primary action (such as \"Renew contract\") and puts other actions such as edit or terminate in a secondary or overflow position": 100,
        "Vendor contacts show each person's name and role, with email as a `mailto:` link and phone as a `tel:` link, and the primary contact is marked with text": 100,
        "Payment milestones show the due date, amount and status, with amounts right-aligned in tabular figures and formatted as currency, and the milestones are ordered with overdue and due-soon ones first": 100,
        "Overdue or upcoming milestones are marked with a text label (such as \"Overdue\" or \"Due in 5 days\"), not by colour alone": 100,
        "The renewal or expiry date is shown as an absolute date with the remaining time stated in words (such as \"Expires in 45 days\")": 100,
        "Amendments are listed with number, date, a short summary and who approved them, using absolute dates": 100,
        "Each section has an empty state with a next action (such as \"Add contact\" or \"Add amendment\"), a loading state, and an inline error with retry": 50,
        "Terminating the contract asks for confirmation that names the contract and the consequence, with a verb button label and focus not on the destructive button": 100,
        "The form is split into titled sections (personal, job and contract, bank and tax, emergency contact, documents) in a single column, with a visible label above every field and no placeholder-only labels": 50,
        "Required fields are marked consistently, and optional fields are labelled as optional or left unmarked by a stated convention": 100,
        "Field widths match their content: dates, postal codes and tax codes are narrow; inputs use the right types (email, tel, date)": 100,
        "An option to save the form as a draft is offered, and saving a draft does not demand every required field": 100,
        "Save and Cancel stay reachable while scrolling (a sticky bar or equivalent), Save is a verb label and is not disabled before submitting": 100,
        "Fields validate on blur and on submit; with several errors a summary at the top links to each field and focus moves to the first invalid field": 100,
        "Leaving the page with unsaved input triggers a warning": 100,
        "The document upload states accepted file types and the size limit, lists chosen files with a remove button, and is keyboard operable": 100,
        "Success is confirmed with a message that names the employee and is announced to assistive technology": 100
      }
    }
